          "filename": "Vimanmek Palace stage.jpg",
          "caption": "Vimanmek Palace (พระที่นั่งวิมานเมฆ), Bangkok, Thailand. The largest building created completely from teak wood. Built 1900-01 is was the residence of King Chulalongkorn (Rama V) 1901-05. Used as the residence for other members of the royal family it fell in disuse in 1932, and was reconstructed to a museum in 1982.\nView from the south, near the \"stage\". Photo by User:Ahoerstemeier on April 3 2001.",
